{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b50aa08747432b6990778eaf7f67239122c5c98828d35b03c7eda511fe261adb","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler outbound comments","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py","fit_for_send()","FittedComment","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fit_for_send.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","# comment-fit-ok:","sanitize_comment","to_wire"],"problem_keywords":["construct-uniqueness guard","fit-dedup-key derivation","duplicate computation","consolidation verification","comment send fit"],"propositions":["The consolidation of outbound-comment fit/dedup-key derivation into fit_for_send() lacks a construct-uniqueness guard required by the parent epic's acceptance criteria, leaving the implementation vulnerable to re-implementation in other modules.","The guard must scan src/rebar except outbound_comments.py and detect the conjunction of fit call and marker-stripped decode producing the dedup key, rejecting unmarked duplicates and bare reasonless markers while accepting marked duplicates with mandatory reasons.","The marker pattern # comment-fit-ok: requires a non-empty reason field; reasonless markers and unmarked duplicate derivations must cause test failures.","The legitimate second fit derivation in the Cloud adapter's add_comment must be marked with # comment-fit-ok: and a mandatory reason to pass the guard."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787805833077055001,"uuid":"b651e69d-9dbf-489c-924b-03cad18553c5"}